WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.863 --> 00:00:11.991
Last year, a certain place in my city, 
Jakarta, was attacked by a suicide bomber.

00:00:11.991 --> 00:00:16.352
Let’s imagine this event happened 
inside a superhero comic book.

00:00:16.352 --> 00:00:21.450
The villain, in this case, 
a suicide bomber, arrives at the scene.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:25.402
He walks around, 
surveying the people and the place.

00:00:25.402 --> 00:00:31.333
Once he is settled, all he needs to do 
is press this little the red button

00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:33.515
and "boom," everything blows up,

00:00:33.515 --> 00:00:36.042
people are running away, 
kids are screaming,

00:00:36.042 --> 00:00:41.453
police and ambulance sirens 
can be heard from every direction.

00:00:41.453 --> 00:00:48.626
Suddenly, the superhero with his cape or
her shining armor comes and saves the day.

00:00:48.626 --> 00:00:53.232
They help civilians to safety, 
puts out the fire,

00:00:53.232 --> 00:00:55.307
takes the injured to a hospital,

00:00:55.307 --> 00:00:59.582
and most importantly, defeats the villain.

00:00:59.582 --> 00:01:01.714
We all love these stories, don't we?

00:01:01.714 --> 00:01:06.393
We all grew up hearing stories of heroism,
especially superheroes -

00:01:06.393 --> 00:01:10.365
how Captain America with all his loyalty 
and super strength,

00:01:10.365 --> 00:01:14.552
he can save the world 
and win hearts of everyone,

00:01:14.552 --> 00:01:22.103
and how Batman using all his money creates
super gadgets to save his city, Gotham.

00:01:22.103 --> 00:01:25.378
Tell me, who doesn’t love them?

00:01:25.378 --> 00:01:29.582
Who doesn’t dream to be saved by them
even though you know they’re fictional?

00:01:29.582 --> 00:01:32.233
Admit it, all of you 
must have dreamt about it.

00:01:32.233 --> 00:01:37.563
But those heroes, the Avengers, 
Batman, Superman,

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:41.013
they have their own place to be a hero.

00:01:41.013 --> 00:01:45.724
They have their own stories where they put
up their shining armor or capes or tights

00:01:45.724 --> 00:01:49.093
and you know, save the world.

00:01:49.093 --> 00:01:53.234
But in the end, they are only stories.

00:01:53.234 --> 00:01:57.473
They don't exist 
in the real world we live in.

00:01:57.473 --> 00:02:02.271
So who then,
are the everyday heroes among us?

00:02:02.271 --> 00:02:06.985
They don’t wear capes or tights 
or have any superpowers

00:02:06.985 --> 00:02:09.832
so what do they look like?

00:02:09.832 --> 00:02:12.720
The dictionary says a hero is someone

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:18.812
who is admired for their courage, noble
qualities and outstanding achievements.

00:02:18.813 --> 00:02:27.184
But to me, I think that heroes are people 
who have the courage to help other people.

00:02:27.184 --> 00:02:29.092
As simple as that.

00:02:29.092 --> 00:02:34.806
It can be if the person just smiles at a
stranger, to me that is an act of heroism.

00:02:34.806 --> 00:02:36.104
Why?

00:02:36.104 --> 00:02:38.974
Because we never know 
what the person might be going through

00:02:38.974 --> 00:02:42.360
and smiling at a stranger 
takes strength and effort.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:46.483
It takes effort to put aside 
our doubts of smiling at a stranger.

00:02:46.483 --> 00:02:52.682
It takes strength to share the same 
feelings with others, to have empathy.

00:02:52.682 --> 00:02:56.440
There are a lot of heroes in real life,

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:00.429
Like Malala, Abraham Lincoln, 
Martin Luther King,

00:03:00.429 --> 00:03:05.159
Soekarno, Indonesia’s first president,
and a whole bunch of others.

00:03:05.159 --> 00:03:08.858
And if I ask you what made them a hero,

00:03:08.858 --> 00:03:12.857
most of us will say, 
let's take an example, Malala,

00:03:12.857 --> 00:03:16.821
most of us will say, “She’s a hero because
she fights for girls education,"

00:03:16.821 --> 00:03:20.748
"She’s a hero because 
she sacrificed herself,"

00:03:20.748 --> 00:03:23.300
or maybe another example,
Martin Luther King.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:27.111
“He’s a hero because he fought for freedom
for people of color."

00:03:27.111 --> 00:03:31.100
She fought for this, he fought for that 
and the whole list goes on.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:36.087
But really though,
let’s take a moment and think about it.

00:03:36.087 --> 00:03:39.959
All the heroes I just mentioned 
and the heroes we all know,

00:03:39.959 --> 00:03:42.178
have helped other people.

00:03:42.178 --> 00:03:44.578
Malala helped girls to have education.

00:03:44.578 --> 00:03:47.696
Martin Luther King helped people of color
to gain greater freedom

00:03:47.696 --> 00:03:50.162
and equality in the United States.

00:03:50.162 --> 00:03:55.589
They all believe in equality and that
everyone should get the same chances.

00:03:55.589 --> 00:03:59.570
They have the vision to make 
this world a better place.

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:05.657
You see, as we grow up, 
we realize that life

00:04:05.657 --> 00:04:09.400
is much harder 
and tougher than it looks.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:13.769
And we humans are social creatures.

00:04:13.769 --> 00:04:20.861
We need each other in order to survive,
we need each other in order to live.

00:04:20.861 --> 00:04:23.640
We need each other to be our heroes.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:26.379
Heroes come in different shapes and sizes.

00:04:26.379 --> 00:04:29.979
We don’t need to have superpowers 
to be heroes.

00:04:29.979 --> 00:04:32.795
We don’t need to have 
a lot of money to be heroes.

00:04:32.795 --> 00:04:36.494
We don't need to stand in front of a gun
to be a hero.

00:04:36.494 --> 00:04:40.245
We don’t need to sacrifice ourselves 
to death to be a hero.

00:04:40.245 --> 00:04:45.053
But we do have to be kind 
to be a hero.

00:04:45.053 --> 00:04:48.394
We have to be helpful to be a hero.

00:04:48.394 --> 00:04:51.660
We have to be empathetic to be a hero.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:55.604
We have to do all these things 
and other good things to be a hero.

00:04:55.604 --> 00:05:00.198
These traits seem simple but it 
actually takes time to practice.

00:05:00.198 --> 00:05:06.385
So what if we start practicing for the day
when we can be heroes?

00:05:06.385 --> 00:05:09.874
What if we had a hero-training?

00:05:09.874 --> 00:05:12.592
Going back to what happened 
in Jakarta last year,

00:05:12.592 --> 00:05:16.466
I think that no matter how long we waited

00:05:16.466 --> 00:05:20.504
for that superhero with his cape 
or her shining armor to come,

00:05:20.504 --> 00:05:25.304
they wouldn't because the real hero 
in this event wasn’t them,

00:05:25.304 --> 00:05:29.544
it was the people who decided fear 
wouldn’t bring them down

00:05:29.544 --> 00:05:32.286
and helped other people, instead.

00:05:32.286 --> 00:05:35.653
I used to think my hero 
is Superman and Batman.

00:05:35.653 --> 00:05:42.573
Trust me, no joke. I have this huge photo 
frame filled with my photos and theirs.

00:05:42.573 --> 00:05:50.316
And then as I got older, 
I stare at it and think.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:56.785
I think that there are more people who 
have been there for me through it all.

00:05:56.785 --> 00:06:01.451
And the thing about life, 
it has its own ups and downs

00:06:01.451 --> 00:06:04.314
in which there are some moments 
where we feel like stopping,

00:06:04.314 --> 00:06:07.234
maybe like throwing up.

00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:10.505
But there is someone who shared 
the same ride with me

00:06:10.505 --> 00:06:15.285
through my ups and down 
and that is my mother.

00:06:15.285 --> 00:06:22.754
She has no cape, no superpowers, 
no exploding bank account.

00:06:22.754 --> 00:06:26.044
She is just another human being.

00:06:26.044 --> 00:06:28.332
But she is there for me.

00:06:28.332 --> 00:06:31.663
She guided me and she helped me.

00:06:31.663 --> 00:06:35.115
She is the reason
I am standing here today,

00:06:35.115 --> 00:06:38.552
so can I say that she is my hero?

00:06:38.552 --> 00:06:41.048
Yes, I can.

00:06:41.048 --> 00:06:43.853
I looked around at how 
I might become a hero,

00:06:43.853 --> 00:06:49.564
and the best example I could find 
wasn’t wearing a cape - it was my mother.

00:06:49.564 --> 00:06:52.427
She is a hero because she's there 
for me to rely on.

00:06:52.427 --> 00:06:56.205
She is a hero because she's there 
for me to wipe away my tears.

00:06:56.205 --> 00:07:01.926
She is my hero because she is there 
for me to make me smile.

00:07:01.926 --> 00:07:06.204
This is just one story we can take 
into our hero-training,

00:07:06.204 --> 00:07:11.984
and I wanted to figure out this hero
formula so that I can share with you all.

00:07:11.984 --> 00:07:13.734
So I did an experiment.

00:07:13.734 --> 00:07:16.514
I spent three days looking 
for hero-makers.

00:07:16.514 --> 00:07:19.094
Here’s what I saw.

00:07:19.094 --> 00:07:21.974
One day, my friend was crying in class.

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:26.404
People around her were telling her 
"to get over it, don't think about it,

00:07:26.404 --> 00:07:29.605
it doesn't matter, you're overreacting."

00:07:29.605 --> 00:07:33.660
But then this other friend came to her 
and gave her a hug.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:39.385
Just support, no advice, 
no talking, just support.

00:07:39.385 --> 00:07:41.465
That's hero lesson number one.

00:07:41.465 --> 00:07:45.044
Heroes are always looking out for others.

00:07:45.044 --> 00:07:47.443
My friend didn’t tell her 
what she should feel

00:07:47.443 --> 00:07:51.363
because to be honest the only one 
who know how it truly feels

00:07:51.363 --> 00:07:53.483
is my friend who was crying.

00:07:53.483 --> 00:07:58.003
So instead, she thought about what 
she might need at that moment.

00:07:58.003 --> 00:08:00.324
That’s empathy.

00:08:00.324 --> 00:08:05.403
The second example is my school nurse was
walking down the street with her baby

00:08:05.403 --> 00:08:07.504
and a toddler beside her.

00:08:07.504 --> 00:08:10.109
She struggled to put everything 
onto her motorbike,

00:08:10.109 --> 00:08:13.375
but then when she finally managed 
to put her children in,

00:08:13.375 --> 00:08:18.964
she almost dropped her bag until a man
came to her and decided to help her.

00:08:18.964 --> 00:08:21.894
That's hero lesson number two.

00:08:21.894 --> 00:08:26.544
Sometimes it doesn’t require 
a great action to be a hero.

00:08:26.544 --> 00:08:32.144
A small gesture like this deserves 
to be called a hero action.

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:36.233
There are a lot more stories 
we can learn from

00:08:36.233 --> 00:08:38.952
and we can add into our hero training,

00:08:38.952 --> 00:08:42.403
But there is one lesson that 
I learned from these events

00:08:42.403 --> 00:08:49.382
and that is sometimes the small gestures 
are the ones that matter the most.

00:08:49.382 --> 00:08:52.773
It is the way we smile at others
that can make us a hero.

00:08:52.773 --> 00:08:54.295
Because you would never know,

00:08:54.295 --> 00:08:57.994
maybe our smile is the only
good thing they had that day.

00:08:57.994 --> 00:09:01.992
It was the way we hug our family 
and friends that makes us a hero.

00:09:01.992 --> 00:09:04.350
It is the way we give a hand to others

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:06.670
when they needed help 
with their groceries.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:13.762
It is the way we make somebody else smile 
that makes us a hero.

00:09:13.762 --> 00:09:19.022
So I think that being a hero isn’t all 
about having a lot of money

00:09:19.022 --> 00:09:22.721
or wearing capes or wearing shining armor

00:09:22.721 --> 00:09:25.708
and doing great things 
and changing the world.

00:09:25.708 --> 00:09:37.031
I think that being a hero is about being 
kind, helpful, generous, and empathetic.

00:09:37.031 --> 00:09:40.663
These are the things we should 
do in our hero training.

00:09:40.663 --> 00:09:45.271
These are the things we should do 
in our daily life as a good human being

00:09:45.271 --> 00:09:48.300
and as a hero.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:51.393
Now, we can all start training today.

00:09:51.393 --> 00:09:54.751
Do you want to be your version 
of Captain Kindness?

00:09:54.751 --> 00:09:59.043
Or maybe you want to have 
your own empathetic-mobile like Batman?

00:09:59.043 --> 00:10:03.651
Or maybe you can be everything by yourself
and be an Avenger.

00:10:03.651 --> 00:10:05.352
It is all up to you.

00:10:05.352 --> 00:10:10.632
If the answer to these questions 
is yes then you know what you have to do.

00:10:10.632 --> 00:10:14.901
Go out there, pick a color of your cape,
and be a hero.

00:10:14.901 --> 00:10:16.289
Thank you.

